{"updated": "2026-08-07T15:09:31.423990+00:00", "fetched": 9, "cache_hits": 5, "bundles": {"7a2093974581": {"label": "cross-asset \u00b7 13 series \u2191", "level": "red", "score": 9.91, "members": ["comex_gold", "comex_silver", "stoxx_50", "cac_40", "dyn_nvda", "dyn_vt", "dax", "sp500", "dow_jones", "russell_2000", "vix", "comex_copper", "gold_silver_ratio"], "articles": [{"title": "Keralam jewellers seek review of gold, silver import duty structure", "feed": "BusinessLine Mkts", "ts": "2026-08-07T14:10:22+00:00", "url": "https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/gold/kerala-jewellers-seek-review-of-gold-silver-import-duty-structure/article71275849.ece", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "The Kerala Gold and Silver Merchants Association (KGSMA) has urged the Centre to immediately review and rationalise the existing import duty structure on gold and silver, warning that higher duties are fuelling smuggling and hurting the legitimate bullion and jewellery trade.\n\nGovernment data presented in Parliament indicate a sharp rise in gold and silver smuggling following the increase in import duty on the precious metals from 6 per cent to 15 per cent, according to S. Abdul Nazar, State General Secretary of the association.\n\nHe said that gold smuggling cases have increased significantly since the duty hike, while silver smuggling has witnessed an even steeper rise, with seizures increas", "citation": "Keralam jewellers seek review of gold, silver import duty structure \u2014 BusinessLine Mkts, 2026-08-07. https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/gold/kerala-jewellers-seek-review-of-gold-silver-import-duty-structure/article71275849.ece"}, {"title": "Silver futures decline to \u20b92.17 lakh/kg", "feed": "BusinessLine Mkts", "ts": "2026-08-07T14:01:41+00:00", "url": "https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/gold/silver-futures-decline-to-217-lakhkg/article71275702.ece", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "Globally, the white metal was trading 1.95 per cent down at $57.22 per ounce in New York. | Photo Credit: istock.com\n\nSilver prices on Tuesday fell by Rs 3,576 to Rs 2,17,597 per kilogram in futures trade as participants reduced their bets.\n\nOn the Multi Commodity Exchange, silver contracts for September delivery declined by Rs 3,576, or 1.62 per cent, to Rs 2,17,597 per kg in a business turnover of 1,716 lots.\n\nAnalysts said a sell-off by participants mainly weighed on silver prices.\n\nGlobally, the white metal was trading 1.95 per cent down at USD 57.22 per ounce in New York.\n\nComments have to be in English, and in full sentences. They cannot be abusive or personal. Please abide by our comm", "citation": "Silver futures decline to \u20b92.17 lakh/kg \u2014 BusinessLine Mkts, 2026-08-07. https://www.thehindubusinessline.com/markets/gold/silver-futures-decline-to-217-lakhkg/article71275702.ece"}, {"title": "Wall Street: S&P 500, Nasdaq edge higher after jobs data", "feed": "Mint Markets", "ts": "2026-08-07T13:56:34+00:00", "url": "https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-news/wall-street-s-p-500-nasdaq-edge-higher-after-jobs-data-11786110178723.html", "status": "ok", "excerpt": "The S&P 500 and the Nasdaq edged higher on Friday after data showed the US economy unexpectedly shed jobs last month, raising doubts about a September interest-rate hike by the Federal Reserve.\n\nAt the open, the Dow Jones Industrial Average fell 35.8 points, or 0.07%, to 53849.26. The S&P 500 rose 25.2 points, or 0.33%, to 7735.18\u200b, while the Nasdaq Composite rose 186.3 points, or 0.71%, to 26534.66.\n\nWith a distinguished career spanning nearly two decades at the highest levels of financial journalism, Rajendra Kumar Saxena stands as a cornerstone of the editorial leadership team at Livemint.com. In his current capacity as Content Editor, he is responsible for managing the comprehensive edit", "citation": "Wall Street: S&P 500, Nasdaq edge higher after jobs data \u2014 Mint Markets, 2026-08-07. https://www.livemint.com/market/stock-market-ne